 Temperature versus pressure for Jupiter. - Realistict top and constant N in the bottom.
 Data from Seiff et al, 1997, ``Thermal structure of Jupiter's upper atmosphere derived from the
 Galileo Probe,'' Science 276, 102-104.  Data for p > 335.30 mbar from orton.dat.
 Seiff data have been smoothed with 2*5+1 boxcar average.
 NOTE: The third column is needed for the file's format, but used rarely in some Newtonian cooling schemes.
